 Never discard the `CompletableFuture<Void>` returned by `Fluxzero.index(...)` from a `void` tracked projection handler. The handler may finish and its consumer may advance before an asynchronous storage failure is observed. For straightforward projections, use `prepareIndex(...).indexAndWait()`. Use the blocking stored variant when the consumer position must wait for indexing. Merely returning a future does not provide that tracking-position guarantee in this version.
 
